    "Microsoft.VSTS.Scheduling.DueDate": "2026-09-22T20:00:00Z",
    "Microsoft.VSTS.TCM.ReproSteps": "An employee originally submitted a leave request for **03/09/2026** on **27/07/2026**. The leave was subsequently cancelled on **30/07/2026**.\n\nAfter the cancellation, there is no longer an effective approved leave for **03/09/2026** in F&amp;O. \n\n![image.png](https://dev.azure.com/gemseducation/c153c9a8-3abc-4dd1-b615-03f718b00c76/_apis/wit/attachments/09b1923f-69bd-4e88-a653-2357767a934c?fileName=image.png) \n\nHowever, when checking **WebESS &gt; Time and Attendance**, the date is still displayed as **Approved Leave**.\n\n![image.png](https://dev.azure.com/gemseducation/c153c9a8-3abc-4dd1-b615-03f718b00c76/_apis/wit/attachments/2fa3ef36-6bfa-4b70-be57-30968223deee?fileName=image.png) \n\nFurther investigation in the **Leave Request Detail** shows that there are multiple transactions for the same employee and leave date:\n*   The original leave transaction created on **27/07/2026** has **Amount = 1** and **Status = Completed**.\n*   A later transaction created on **30/07/2026** for the cancellation has **Amount = 0** and **Status = Completed**.\n\n![image.png](https://dev.azure.com/gemseducation/c153c9a8-3abc-4dd1-b615-03f718b00c76/_apis/wit/attachments/99e9ee10-5d26-4e0a-a3c0-9286354ca987?fileName=image.png) \n\nTherefore, checking only whether a Leave Request has **Status = Completed** can result in the original leave being displayed even though it was subsequently cancelled.\n\n### Actual Result\n\n**03/09/2026** is still displayed as **Approved Leave** in WebESS &gt; Time and Attendance after the leave has been cancelled.\n\n### Expected Logic\n\n*   Match the leave by **Employee + Leave Date**.\n*   Check the corresponding **Leave Request Detail**.\n*   Consider the **latest effective transaction** for the leave date.\n*   If the leave was subsequently cancelled (**Amount = 0**), the date should **no longer be considered as leave**, even if the original request remains **Completed**.\n*   Only display **Approved Leave** when the leave is still effective for that date.",
